{"content":[{"c":["ARKITE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Name of a clan descended from Ham’s son Canaan (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.10.17","r":"Gen.10.17","rawR":"Gen.10.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.10.17","value":"Gen.10.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 10:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.15","r":"1Chr.1.15","rawR":"1Chr.1.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.15","value":"1Chr.1.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:15"},"). The Arkites were probably residents of Arqa, a Phoenician town north of Tripolis in Syria. According to an early inscription, Arqa was captured by the Assyrian Tiglath-pileser III in 738 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". Possibly another branch of the tribe settled near Ataroth, a town on the border between Ephraim and Benjamin (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.16.2","r":"Josh.16.2","rawR":"Josh.16.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.16.2","value":"Josh.16.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 16:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=ArchiArchite_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"ArchiArchite_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"ArchiArchite_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Archi, Archite"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Arkite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 10:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.10.17","rawQueryValue":"Gen.10.17","sourceRefExact":"Gen.10.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.15","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.15","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.15"},{"anchorText":"Jos 16:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.16.2","rawQueryValue":"Josh.16.2","sourceRefExact":"Josh.16.2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e61d3708bb252b7e